Subject: WPE on Phoenix: <video>/<audio> without GStreamer, a media player over FFmpeg (USE_FFMPEG)

WPE ties video to GStreamer by one CMake rule (GStreamerDependencies.cmake:
ENABLE_VIDEO depends on USE_GSTREAMER); WebCore's media code itself has non-GStreamer,
non-Cocoa paths, and the engine registry, the compositor's buffer proxy and the layer buffer
types are generic. This patch adds a WPE option USE_FFMPEG (private, OFF; depends on
ENABLE_VIDEO, conflicts with USE_GSTREAMER) and, with it, a media engine over FFmpeg's
libraries (platform/graphics/ffmpeg/, BSD-2-Clause):

  MediaPlayerPrivateFFmpeg              demux thread (libavformat) -> packet queues -> video and
                                        audio threads; a pausable wall clock as the master,
                                        audio (libswresample, 44.1 kHz S16 stereo) written to
                                        /dev/audio0 and following it; pictures wait for their
                                        time or are dropped when late; seek, end, volume, mute
  FFmpegMediaStream                     the bytes: file:// read directly, the rest through
                                        WebKit's media resource loader (Range requests on seek)
  CoordinatedPlatformLayerBufferFFmpeg  a decoded 8-bit 4:2:0 picture for the compositor, its
                                        planes uploaded and converted on the GPU: Skia
                                        (TextureFromYUVAPixmaps) or TextureMapper's YUV shader

HEVC goes to whatever avcodec_find_decoder() returns: with the video_player port's FFmpeg that
is hevc_rpivid, the decoder on the Pi 4's rpivid block. Not supported: Media Source Extensions,
Web Audio, WebCodecs, encrypted media, rates other than 1, painting into a canvas.

Every event prints "WPEB-MEDIA mono=<ms> id=<n> ..." on stderr; WPE_PHOENIX_MEDIA_STAT_MS
(default 2000, 0 off) is the period of the "stat" line; WPE_PHOENIX_MEDIA_THREADS sets the
decoders' thread count (0: FFmpeg's choice), WPE_PHOENIX_MEDIA_AUDIO=0 keeps the device closed.

Also: GStreamer.cmake adds GStreamer's sources only with USE_GSTREAMER; the new engine
identifier and player type (+ the IPC serializer list, the remote player's switch); and
VideoFrame.cpp's non-GStreamer fallback includes NativeImage.h (copyNativeImage() returns a
RefPtr<NativeImage>: it compiled only where a unified bundle happened to include it).

